processing of CAAX-type prenylated proteins. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9Y256","text":"Protease involved in the processing of a variety of prenylated proteins containing the C-terminal CAAX motif, where C is a cysteine modified with an isoprenoid lipid, A is an aliphatic amino acid and X is any C-terminal amino acid. Proteolytically removes the C-terminal three residues of farnesylated and geranylated proteins, leaving the prenylated cysteine as the new C-terminus. Is able to process K-Ras, N-Ras, H-Ras, RAP1B and G-gamma-1 (PubMed:10085068)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}